tion and conventions","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:a9296035bf75deaaf999eb04a5915e3dde7e0cdcdfae5d3c2a19703323764325","file":"preprints/Strong-diffeomorphic-approximation-in-three-dimensions-for-p-gt-2-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":25,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"826aceddd630476dbf74659aedfcff38775b04c15bd7becdd691690ce0b552c1","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Strong-diffeomorphic-approximation-in-three-dimensions-for-p-gt-2-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:a9296035bf75deaaf999eb04a5915e3dde7e0cdcdfae5d3c2a19703323764325","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Strong-diffeomorphic-approximation-in-three-dimensions-for-p-gt-2-September-24-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L25"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{main:theorem}\\label{ha:approximation}\nLet $\\Omega,\\Lambda\\subset\\R^3$ be bounded domains, let $2<p<\\infty$,\nand let $f:\\Omega\\to\\Lambda$ be a homeomorphism in\n$W^{1,p}(\\Omega;\\R^3)$. There exist $C^\\infty$ diffeomorphisms\n$f_j:\\Omega\\to\\Lambda$, each belonging to\n$W^{1,p}(\\Omega;\\R^3)$, such that\n\\begin{equation}\\label{main:convergence}\n\\int_\\Omega\\bigl( |f_j-f|^p+|Df_j-Df|^p\\bigr)\\,dx\\longrightarrow0.\n\\end{equation}"}
